    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Luis Arraez** (66.15) and **Daulton Varsho** (65.84) anchor our lineup, representing our highest-ceiling plays against favorable matchups. **Luis Arraez** benefits from an elite leadoff spot and a 4.86 xERA matchup against Civale, providing a high floor for batting average, while **Daulton Varsho** maximizes his scoring potential through a strong dynamic platoon edge (+10%) against Lambert. We are also high on **Taylor Ward** (64.16), whose leadoff positioning and a soft matchup against Johnson (5.15 xERA) make him a premium start despite a slight platoon drag. While **Cal Raleigh** (64.83) faces a moderate 4.45 xERA arm, his high-leverage spot in the #2 hole and solid SP skill adjustment solidify his place as a core contributor.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Drew Gilbert** (51.88), who narrowly missed the cut behind the consistent production profiles of **Jeremiah Jackson** and **Geraldo Perdomo**. While **Drew Gilbert** benefited from the same positive SP skill indicators as the rest of the team against Civale, his lower spot in the order (#8) and marginal base projection limited his efficiency score relative to our starters. We are closely monitoring the status of **Gavin Sheets**, whose 60.46 score is bolstered by a massive +19% SP skill boost against Ritchie, though we remain wary of his reliance on platoon splits. With **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Will Smith** sidelined on the IL and **Ryan Waldschmidt** still developing in Reno, we are managing our remaining depth carefully to preserve game caps while hunting for the stolen bases that remain our primary objective for the season.",
